        {
          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"version\":\"design_judgment_v1\",\"case_key\":\"223d00bffbb05674e0efd936\",\"status\":\"scored\",\"units\":[{\"unit_id\":\"step_1\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Required to establish the exposure before applying the approval threshold.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0009\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0000\"}],\"rationale\":\"Several accounts require balance retrieval, dated conversions, reconciliation of inconsistent currency identifiers, and aggregation.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":3,\"tool_use\":3,\"information\":3}},{\"unit_id\":\"step_2\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Threshold comparison and the applicable endpoint are required; the approval request applies only if the computed exposure exceeds the threshold.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0008\"}],\"rationale\":\"The step branches on the computed exposure and, if approval is required, on its response. Recording must link the source balances and conversions and must not occur after rejection.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":3,\"tool_use\":3,\"information\":2}}],\"dimensions\":{\"workload\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The sufficient path entails multi-account discovery, balance and rate retrieval, reconciliation, calculation, and an endpoint decision. Approval and recording are counted only on branches where required; work after a rejection is excluded.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0000\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0009\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0008\"}]},\"reasoning\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Currency-identifier discrepancies and dated conversions must be reconciled before applying the threshold and approval rule.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0009\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0000\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"}]},\"tool_use\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Account identifiers, balances, currencies, dated rates, and supporting records must be bound across multiple calls and, on the applicable branch, into an approval request and linked record.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0001\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0009\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"}]},\"dependencies\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Balance and rate discovery precede the exposure decision. If approval is required, its response determines whether to record or report rejection; rejection is a decisive exit, with no subsequent reconciliation. The unknown exposure makes both threshold branches possible, not cumulative work.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0009\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0008\"}]},\"information\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The task requires finding linked accounts and their balances and dated rates, then resolving inconsistent currency identifiers; the exposure and applicable approval branch are not supplied.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0000\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0009\"}]}},\"overall_score\":75,\"intended_endpoint\":{\"description\":\"Record a linked reconciliation preserving the source balances and conversions with approval when required, or report a rejected approval without recording the reconciliation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0008\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"}]},\"dependency_reasoning\":\"A sufficient path first discovers accounts, balances, and applicable rates, resolves identifiers, and computes exposure. That establishes whether approval is mandatory. If requested approval is rejected, reporting rejection is the decisive exit and recording is excluded; otherwise the applicable linked reconciliation is recorded. No ordering among account-level retrievals is prescribed.\",\"score_rationale\":\"Substantial multi-account work and cross-record binding, with meaningful currency reconciliation and an approval-dependent endpoint, support five level-3 ratings: 5 × (3+3+3+3+3) = 75.\",\"uncertainties\":[\"The balances and resulting exposure are not supplied, so whether approval is required cannot be determined from the sources.\",\"The form of the inconsistent currency identifiers and how they can be resolved are unspecified.\",\"The sources do not establish whether a requested approval would be granted or rejected.\"],\"source_quality_flags\":[\"The tool contract lists record_balance, but the workflow and endpoint do not specify a separate balance-recording obligation; it is not counted as required work.\"],\"unscorable_reason\":\"\"}",
          "type": "output_text",
          "logprobs": []
        }
